# HomeAsset talks to the local SQLite API on your computer — there is no Supabase.
#
# Env var name (required on a physical phone):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL
#
# Simulator / Expo Go on the same PC: leave unset (defaults to http://localhost:8787).
#
# Physical phone or tablet on Wi‑Fi — set your PC's LAN IPv4 (NOT localhost, NOT 127.0.0.1):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8787
#
# Windows — find the IP:
#   1. Open Command Prompt
#   2. Run: ipconfig
#   3. Under "Wireless LAN adapter Wi-Fi" (or Ethernet), copy IPv4 Address
#   4. Put it in apps/mobile/.env as above (keep port 8787)
#   5. Save the file, then restart Expo: npx expo start --go -c
#
# Phone and PC must be on the same Wi‑Fi. Allow Node.js through Windows Firewall if Windows asks.
